From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: K11MCH1 <81425424+K11MCH1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 20:58:32 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] nir/lower_explicit_io: Keep the 32-bit offset wrap with
 offset_shift

With offset_shift, explicit_io_offset_from_deref() shifts the array
stride right before the multiply, so an array term becomes
index * (stride >> shift). The byte offset this replaces,
index * stride, is a 32-bit value that wraps. Pre-shifting keeps the
bits that the wrap would drop, so for a large index
(index * stride mod 2^32) >> shift and index * (stride >> shift)
differ by a multiple of 2^(32 - shift). Only ir3 sets
max_offset_shift, so this affects freedreno and Turnip.

vkd3d-proton emits raw buffer indices that rely on the wrap. Unreal
Engine 5 Nanite's cluster culling stores hardware-raster clusters from
the end of a uvec2 list, and its SPIR-V computes the slot as
0x1fffffff - k + MaxVisibleClusters, that is
(MaxVisibleClusters - 1 - k) + 2^29. Turnip turned that into the dword
offset 2 * (MaxVisibleClusters - 1 - k) + 2^30, 4 GiB past the
binding, so robust buffer access dropped every store. The hardware
rasterizer then read zero records and drew one cluster over and over,
and those surfaces were missing (Lords of the Fallen 2023, UE 5.1).

By SPIR-V rules that index is out of bounds, so dropping the store is
allowed. Masking the shifted term with UINT32_MAX >> shift for 32-bit
offsets gives back exactly the result of the wrapped byte offset, as
before offset_shift.

Tested on Adreno 840 (KGSL):
  A compute shader storing to uvec2[] at 0x1fffffff - k + n
  (n = 1024, robustBufferAccess on): 0/64 stores landed before,
  64/64 at element n - 1 - k after.
  A Lords of the Fallen frame capture replayed on the device:
  hardware-raster cluster records 0/1100 before, 1100/1100 after, and
  the missing geometry is drawn.
No VK-CTS run.

Fixes: 30716cc5243 ("nir/lower_explicit_io: add support for offset_shift")
Fixes: 7752cc26c45 ("ir3: use offset_shift for SSBO intrinsics")
---
 src/compiler/nir/nir_lower_explicit_io.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/compiler/nir/nir_lower_explicit_io.c b/src/compiler/nir/nir_lower_explicit_io.c
index 9367150..f45ba13 100644
--- a/src/compiler/nir/nir_lower_explicit_io.c
+++ b/src/compiler/nir/nir_lower_explicit_io.c
@@ -1246,6 +1246,12 @@ explicit_io_offset_from_deref(nir_builder *b, nir_deref_instr *deref,
          offset = nir_amul_imm(b, index, stride);
       }
 
+      /* Keep ((index * stride) mod 2^32) >> shift: vkd3d-proton raw buffer
+       * indices rely on the 32-bit byte offset wrapping.
+       */
+      if (shift && offset_bit_size == 32)
+         offset = nir_iand_imm(b, offset, UINT32_MAX >> shift);
+
       return offset;
    }
 
